            <title>[LU-21161] ldiskfs: fstrim thread hit BUG_ON at umount and was not started/stopped at remount (fstrim/nofstrim/ro)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21161</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Issue1: thread hit BUG_ON(JBD2_UNMOUNT) at umount&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fstrim thread added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17980" title="improve ldiskfs ongoing TRIM performance" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17980"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17980&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; can start a journal handle while the journal is being destroyed at umount:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
  kernel BUG at fs/jbd2/transaction.c:369!
  CPU: 4 PID: 1649839 Comm: fstrim-sdb 6.12.0-124.28.1.el10_1.x86_64
  RIP: 0010:start_this_handle+0x226/0x500 [jbd2]
  Call Trace:
   jbd2__journal_start+0xfb/0x1f0 [jbd2]
   ldiskfs_try_to_trim_range+0x5ec/0x7e0 [ldiskfs]
   ldiskfs_trim_all_free+0x168/0x1c0 [ldiskfs]
   ldiskfs_mb_fstrim_thread+0x418/0x550 [ldiskfs]
   kthread+0xfd/0x240&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The thread is started in ext4_mb_init() and stopped in ext4_mb_release(), but ext4_put_super() destroys the journal before calling ext4_mb_release(). While trimming, the thread starts a&lt;br/&gt;
journal handle (ldiskfs_try_to_trim_range() -&amp;gt; jbd2__journal_start()) to record the trimmed groups, so if it is still running when jbd2_journal_destroy() has set JBD2_UNMOUNT, start_this_handle() hits the BUG_ON. The same placement also leaks the thread when mount fails after ext4_mb_init() (the failed_mount5 path does not stop it), and leaves it running after "remount,nofstrim", since ext4_mb_release() skips the stop when the option is cleared.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;issue2: thread was not started/stopped at remount:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
a) &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"remount,fstrim"&lt;/span&gt; on a filesystem mounted without fstrim sets the option but never starts the thread. Queued groups are never trimmed, and the allocator keeps skipping them in the fast scan passes.
b) &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"remount,nofstrim"&lt;/span&gt; leaves the thread running until umount.
c) &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"remount,ro"&lt;/span&gt; leaves the thread running. Trimming then hits WARN_ON_ONCE(sb_rdonly(sb)) in ext4_journal_check_start() and gets -EROFS, after which the thread never trims again, even after &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"remount,rw"&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
